From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shikosu <teovidal01@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 22:38:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] horizon on linux: the hot NVN calls are recorded in C

Bindings, viewports, draws, render targets and the setters of state objects are host functions in libnx2linux_gpu.so (linux/host/nvnrec.c) that the recompiled game calls without Python; nvn_rec.py takes each command buffer's stream back as the tuples horizon_nvn.py records itself. NX2LINUX_NVN_NATIVE=0 turns it off. Tests compare the C and Python versions on random arguments. 150 s of Xenoblade Chronicles 2: 637 frames against 517.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: NX2Linux S7bis: the hot NVN calls recorded in C, off the Python bridge
Issue: none yet (NX2Linux, branch swann/jalon-s7bis-xc2)

---
